<!--
  Renders a single "Up next" card below a show view, linking to the
  chronologically-newer post in the same collection. "Next" means
  strictly newer — at the newest post the section is suppressed
  rather than falling back to an older neighbour (which would
  contradict the label).

  Reuses the `_post_list` partial's card markup, so cover and
  per-card toggles inherit from `collections.posts.index` (`show_image`,
  `show_date`, `show_description`, etc.). One card per render.

  Hero behavior:
    - Next post has `image:` → hero renders on the left of the card
      at desktop (≥ 480px), pinned to 240px wide so it matches the
      `.related__cover` thumbnails directly below it. Mobile stacks
      cover-on-top, body-below — same reflow the related grid does
      when there's not enough width for two columns.
    - Next post has no `image:` → no cover renders, card falls back
      to a text-only single-column layout. No placeholder tile —
      it's a single emphasized card, so the visual-consistency
      problem the related grid has (mix of cards) doesn't apply.

  Usage:
      <%%= render 'partials/next_item' %>

  Config (per collection in config/site.yml):

      collections:
        posts:
          next:
            enabled: true       # set false to suppress the section

  Renders nothing when the source is the newest in its collection,
  there's no next page (e.g. the only post in a collection), or
  `next.enabled` is false.
-->
<% next_post = site.next_in_collection(page) %>
<% if next_post %>
<section class="next-item" aria-labelledby="next-item-heading">
  <h2 id="next-item-heading" class="next-item__heading">Up next</h2>
  <%== render 'partials/post_list', posts: [next_post] %>
</section>
<% end %>
